{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792763210,"nonce":"KdZWk4p7RQjXDUpmtxt02pWSrZs=","title":"Isolate native extensions in supervised host processes","message":"Extensions declaring native libraries currently execute inside RayDE and can corrupt or terminate the editor. Route their complete VM and libraries to an individually identifiable headless process, preserving script-only embedded VMs. Reuse serialized extension UI and service messages with nonblocking bounded transport, validate child output, capture bounded stderr diagnostics, and retain native approvals. Stop or disable must terminate and reap a hung native host after a bounded graceful shutdown. Crash cleanup must release editor-owned views and registrations; supervision must not replay failed commands that could modify files. Package the host beside development and bundled executables. Verify real native crashes, hanging calls, output pressure, cancellation, process reaping, host built-ins and existing Git workflows. Document native memory ownership and the remaining scope of isolation.","files":null}]}